# Project structure explanations
# .clinerules – contains architecture, coding standards, and other rule documents governing the framework.
# .cline/agents – markdown definitions of major agents, each handling a specific responsibility in the automation pipeline.
# .cline/templates – template files used by agents to scaffold artefacts such as features, scenarios, page objects, components, fixtures, etc.
# .cline/prompts – prompt definitions that guide agents when generating content.
# .cline/skills – reusable skill libraries (e.g., Playwright, locator generation) that agents invoke to perform concrete actions.
# Relations: Agents use prompts to decide what to generate, employ skills to implement logic, and output files based on templates. Templates provide the file skeleton, prompts define the generation context, and skills supply the code snippets.

